        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This test that belongs into the category of CSMP-Interface (to other software) tests is not automated! Instead, one needs to run the test code which writes UGX files in ASCII format. These output files must then be checked with ProMesh for whether all the desired features of the CSMP model that is output (2D and 3D examples used here) are captured by the UG version of these models.</para>
<para><xrefsect id="todo_1_todo000269"><xreftitle>Todo</xreftitle><xrefdescription><para>Currently the UG subsets in the subsethandler for CSMP <ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_boundary" kindref="compound">Boundary</ref> objects are not visible in UG, upon visual examination the file-based output looks the same as for the successful output of <ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_region" kindref="compound">Region</ref> objects. </para>
</xrefdescription></xrefsect></para>
        </detaileddescription>
